  "schema": "arcpuzzles-parametric-prototype-evidence-v1",
  "scope": "# Review 4ca8a7b38652 v3.0.0 \u2014 review-739adb393a726593\nDefect \u2192 repair: the isolated count-scope prototype now supports independent demo/query counts, rejects duplicate inputs, and exports exact-hash Racket files and strictly public challenges.\nCanonical generator unchanged: `9e39ddd0012e5dba7be9e7ae10f3ac8de0ca736e8c7bfad79a3535b4ae352ac5`; canonical Racket authority unchanged, `RULE_HASH=2e2cb8677499`.\nFinal canonical checks: 12/12 battery stages green; separate task tests 37/37 passed; fresh replay also passed 37 task tests plus 28 tooling tests.\nProduction lessons: five ordered demos; 300/300 lessons passed, with all 1,800 single-query rotations passed under required-rotation policy (1,656 unique inputs).\nSchedule enumeration: all five start residues at seed 0 across three bands; 15 lessons, 90 rotations, 27 unique inputs; no ambiguity or warnings.\nFour-query production: seed 17, five demos plus four distinct queries, nine distinct accepted inputs, nine Racket labels, all four demo-only lesson checks passed; three Racket process-death rejections retained.\nProposed parameter extension: two fixed count-scope settings; six episodes, 28 demos, 24 queries, 52 distinct inputs and 104 retained Racket evaluations; every query identifiable from demos.\nBlind/exposed solves: one revision each; 3/3 and 5/5 visible examples passed; hidden-query correctness remains unknown, exposure declarations retained.\nAcceptance: needs attention \u2014 approve the task-local prototype/tool proposal separately; the return uses a reviewed optional archive-backed builder because stock packaging requires a full physical checkout.\nRemaining scope: finite rivals and bounded seeds, unchanged 3\u00d73 domain, audit targets findings-only, no new training admission; final replay status is recorded below and in RESULTS.json.\n\n## Delivered work and findings\n",
